hip-virtual-mem-release: a fix to intel/llvm's virtual memory of the HIP adapter (hip-virtual-mem, intel/llvm's
c13ad6c7e3 on v7.2.0), applied by tools/intel_llvm_build.py.

With a ROCr that leaves its own mapping at an unmapped range, the physical memory of a range unmapped with
hipMemUnmap stayed allocated after hipMemRelease: the device's free memory did not grow, another program
could not take it, and another allocation of this process took other memory (ROCm 7.1.1 on the RX 9060 XT:
4 GiB mapped, unmapped and released left the driver's used VRAM at 4334 MiB of the 238 MiB before; ROCm 10.1
went back to 238 MiB).  XeStrata's --vram-elastic could not lend its segments to an image job there (the
engine sees it at start and refuses), and the draft head parked for a prompt made no room.

ROCr maps the physical memory to the CPU at the range, inaccessible, when it maps it to the GPU, a mapping of
the DRM device.  ROCm 7.1.1's ROCr does not take it away at the unmap, and it holds the memory until the
range is mapped again or freed; ROCm 10.1's makes the range an anonymous mapping again.  Fixed,
urVirtualMemUnmap looks, after the first unmap, at what /proc/self/maps shows at the range: where it is still
the DRM device's, it makes every unmapped range the reservation it was, the anonymous inaccessible mapping
ROCr reserves a range with, and the memory goes back when it is released; where it is anonymous (or the line
is not found, or is of another file) it does nothing.  What the runtime does decides, not its version, and
UR_LOG_HIP=level:info says which it was.
---
diff --git a/unified-runtime/source/adapters/hip/virtual_mem.cpp b/unified-runtime/source/adapters/hip/virtual_mem.cpp
--- a/unified-runtime/source/adapters/hip/virtual_mem.cpp
+++ b/unified-runtime/source/adapters/hip/virtual_mem.cpp
@@ -6,19 +6,80 @@
 // SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0 WITH LLVM-exception
 //
 // Modified 2026 by MistVVK and the XeStrata contributors: the GPU's
-// translations of an unmapped range dropped (dropStaleTranslations).
+// translations of an unmapped range dropped (dropStaleTranslations); an
+// unmapped range made a reservation again where the runtime leaves its mapping
+// there (leavesCpuMapping).
 //
 //===----------------------------------------------------------------------===//
 
 #include "common.hpp"
 #include "context.hpp"
 #include "event.hpp"
+#include "logger/ur_logger.hpp"
 #include "physical_mem.hpp"
 
 #include <cassert>
 
+#if defined(__linux__)
+#include <atomic>
+#include <cstdio>
+#include <cstring>
+#include <sys/mman.h>
+#endif
+
 namespace {
 
+#if defined(__linux__)
+// Whether hipMemUnmap leaves ROCr's mapping of the physical memory at the
+// range, by what the first unmapped range shows.
+//
+// ROCr maps the physical memory to the CPU at the range, inaccessible, when it
+// maps it to the GPU. A ROCr that does not take that mapping away at the unmap
+// (ROCm 7.1.1's; 10.1's does) keeps the physical memory allocated after
+// hipMemRelease, until the range is mapped again or freed: the device's free
+// memory does not grow, and another allocation takes other memory. The mapping
+// shows in /proc/self/maps as one of the DRM device (/dev/dri/...), where a
+// reservation is anonymous. It is looked up after the first unmap and kept, as
+// a runtime does one or the other. A range whose line is not found, or is of
+// another file, is left alone: what is there is not known to be ROCr's to
+// replace, and all that is lost is the memory's return.
+bool leavesCpuMapping(const void *pStart) {
+  static std::atomic<int> Leaves{-1};
+  int Known = Leaves.load(std::memory_order_relaxed);
+  if (Known >= 0)
+    return Known != 0;
+  Known = 0;
+  const char *What = "not found in /proc/self/maps: left as it is";
+  if (std::FILE *Maps = std::fopen("/proc/self/maps", "r")) {
+    const unsigned long Addr = reinterpret_cast<unsigned long>(pStart);
+    char Line[512];
+    while (std::fgets(Line, sizeof Line, Maps)) {
+      unsigned long Lo = 0, Hi = 0, Inode = 0;
+      int PathAt = 0;
+      if (std::sscanf(Line, "%lx-%lx %*4s %*x %*x:%*x %lu %n", &Lo, &Hi, &Inode,
+                      &PathAt) < 3 ||
+          Addr < Lo || Addr >= Hi)
+        continue;
+      if (Inode == 0) {
+        What = "anonymous: the runtime made it a reservation again";
+      } else if (PathAt > 0 &&
+                 std::strncmp(Line + PathAt, "/dev/dri/", 9) == 0) {
+        Known = 1;
+        What = "still mapped to the DRM device: unmapped ranges are made "
+               "reservations again";
+      } else {
+        What = "mapped to another file: left as it is";
+      }
+      break;
+    }
+    std::fclose(Maps);
+  }
+  UR_LOG(INFO, "A range unmapped with hipMemUnmap is {}", What);
+  Leaves.store(Known, std::memory_order_relaxed);
+  return Known != 0;
+}
+#endif
+
 // Makes the GPUs' engines forget the translations of a range that was just
 // unmapped.
 //
@@ -153,6 +214,15 @@
     ScopedDevice Active(hContext->getDevices()[0]);
     UR_CHECK_ERROR(hipMemUnmap(const_cast<void *>(pStart), size));
   }
+#if defined(__linux__)
+  // the reservation the range was: the anonymous, inaccessible mapping ROCr
+  // reserves a range with
+  if (leavesCpuMapping(pStart) &&
+      mmap(const_cast<void *>(pStart), size, PROT_NONE,
+           MAP_PRIVATE | MAP_ANONYMOUS | MAP_FIXED | MAP_NORESERVE, -1,
+           0) == MAP_FAILED)
+    return UR_RESULT_ERROR_OUT_OF_HOST_MEMORY;
+#endif
   dropStaleTranslations(hContext);
   return UR_RESULT_SUCCESS;
 }
